Requirement Analysis

ComicCraft – AI Comic Story Creator Using Gemini Models

1. Introduction

ComicCraft is an AI-powered web application that helps users create comic stories from simple text prompts. The system uses Google Gemini models to generate story content, characters, dialogues, scenes, and comic-panel descriptions. The generated content can then be organized into a complete comic.


---

2. Functional Requirements

FR1 – User Registration and Login

Users can create an account.

Users can log in and log out securely.

User information should be stored in a database.


FR2 – Story Prompt Input

User can enter a story idea or prompt.

User can specify genre, theme, characters, setting, and preferred story length.

The system validates the entered information.


FR3 – AI Story Generation

The system sends the user's prompt to the Gemini API.

Gemini generates the story based on the given requirements.

The system displays the generated story to the user.


FR4 – Character Creation

Users can define characters manually or allow AI to create them.

The system generates character names, personalities, roles, and descriptions.


FR5 – Comic Panel Generation

The story is divided into individual comic panels/scenes.

Each panel contains:

Scene description

Character actions

Dialogue

Narration/captions

Visual-generation prompt



FR6 – Story Editing

Users can edit the generated:

Story

Characters

Dialogues

Scenes

Panel order


Users can regenerate selected sections using AI.


FR7 – Comic Preview

The system provides a visual preview of the complete comic.

Users can navigate between panels.


FR8 – Save and Manage Comics

Users can save generated comics.

Users can view, edit, rename, or delete previous projects.


FR9 – Export

Users can export the completed comic in a suitable format such as PDF or image files.

The exported comic should preserve panel order and text.


FR10 – Error Handling

The system should display appropriate messages when:

Gemini API fails

Internet connection is unavailable

Invalid input is provided

Generation fails or times out




---

3. Non-Functional Requirements

Performance

Story generation should respond within a reasonable time.

The application should load quickly.

The system should support multiple users.


Security

User passwords must be securely protected.

API keys must not be exposed on the client side.

User data should be protected from unauthorized access.


Usability

Interface should be simple and beginner-friendly.

Comic creation should require minimal technical knowledge.

Clear buttons and navigation should be provided.


Reliability

Generated projects should not be lost during normal operation.

Errors should be handled gracefully.


Scalability

The system should allow additional AI models and features to be added later.


Maintainability

The application should use modular components.

Frontend, backend, database, and AI services should be separated logically.



